							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;">i&#039;m glad this is finnaly starting to get some attention on the main tv news stations now.&nbsp; not that i&#039;m surprised it took so long.&nbsp; they won&#039;t cover any racial issues until jesse jackson and al sharpton are making speaches about it.&nbsp; it really pisses me off how one sided and skewed their coverage has been. <br /><br />i saw stories abc nbc cbs local fox, cable fox and cnn on this yesterday.&nbsp; and on all of them their coverage essentiall was that a noose got hung in the school yard, then a bunch of black students beat up a white student, and now there are protests because the black students are on trial for the beating but no white students were charged for hanging the noose, and they left it at that.&nbsp; <br /><br />Well fuck, if that was all i heard about the story, i&#039;d think all the black people protesting this were a bunch of douche bags too.&nbsp; That is comlpetely not the point of the contention or of the protests.&nbsp; At least in the segments i saw on those channels there was no mention that the students were charged with attempted murder for the school fight, that each of them faced 100 year prison sentances and that the district attorney had promised them that he would pursue those maximum sentances.&nbsp; no mention that the day before the fight at school one of the jena 6 had been beaten by the white student who got beat up at school and a group of his friends, and not even an investigation was launched into that incident.&nbsp; not a mention that the district attorney had threatened to ruin the black student&#039;s lives if they didn&#039;t stop protesting the hanging of the noose and demanding prosecution for the act.&nbsp; not a mention that a typical punishment for fighting at school is expulsion not 100 year sentances in federal penetentiary.&nbsp; <br /><br />This isn&#039;t about the hanging of the noose, its about a racist ass district attorney who deserves to be disbarred and tried for prosecutorial misconduct.&nbsp; thats why there are protests, not because people think the jena 6 should be set free because they were responding to a noose getting hung.&nbsp; that has nothing to do with it.&nbsp; people don&#039;t think the jena 6 should not be punnished for assaulting someone at school, they think the punnishments should be just, and that when white students commit the same crime against a black student they should be prosecuted in a similar manner.&nbsp; <br /><br />god i hate TV news.</div>
